=== layout: section

# Collaboration Tips

=== layout: one-panel

# Group Collaboration Tips

@body

- Start early
  - Draft the business plan while working on the presentation
- Don't break up sections by student\:
  - Leads to incoherent, non-cohesive documents
  - I recommend at least two people per section, otherwise some sections won't get done or done well.
- Face-to-face meetings are great, but difficult to coordinate
  - Use video conferencing, i.e., Google Meet or Zoom for easy meetings
- Store documents in the Cloud, e.g., Google Docs
  - Everyone can edit the document at the same time

=== layout: one-panel

# Group Collaboration Tips

@body

- Establish a separate group roles\:
  - [*Coordinator*]{color=#C9211E} = schedule meetings and checks progress of group members
  - [*Leader*]{color=#ba5d00} = assign jobs and decides what content will be included
  - [*Formatter*]{color=#777b08} = creates figures and makes sure the presentation and plan look consistent and nice
  - [*Researcher*]{color=#058929} = reads articles and other sample business plans
  - [*Editor*]{color=#3465A4} = checks the grammar and wording, double check formatting

